9c876479768dd3126","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-22T07:54:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T07:54:01Z"},{"id":665103088,"node_id":"RA_kwDOQwJa6M4npKrw","name":"lazyworktree_Windows_x86_64.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":5786241,"digest":"sha256:d39b7a8f102bad6548747cf50c0293721d6694b0ca30d323e6067ea4ffc29d0b","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-22T07:54:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T07:54:01Z"}],"body":"This release introduces support for the Herdr multiplexer, implements worktree tracking for multiplexer sessions, adds interactive branch checkout and sync improvements, and enhances safety during worktree updates.\n\n### Features\n\n- **Herdr Multiplexer Support**: Added integration for Herdr as a custom command target, supporting both workspace and named-session modes, multi-tab layouts, containerized execution, CLI `exec` support, and a default `H` keybinding.\n- **Worktree-Aware Session Tracking**: Tagged tmux sessions and Herdr workspaces with their associated worktree metadata, allowing sessions to be accurately rediscovered even if session names change.\n- **Interactive Picker Highlights**: Worktrees that are already checked out are now flagged with `[worktree]` and highlighted in green within the `-P` (pull request) and `-I` (issue) interactive selectors.\n- **Direct Branch Checkout**: The `create` command can now check out an existing local or remote-tracking branch directly when no explicit worktree name is specified, falling back to a generated branch name if already in use.\n- **Diverged Worktree Guidance**: Provided suggested `git rebase` and `git reset --hard` commands when existing worktrees cannot be updated due to divergent history.\n- **Safe Worktree Fast-Forwarding**: Enhanced `--update-on-existing` to safely fast-forward clean worktrees to the latest upstream commit rather than performing hard resets, leaving dirty, ahead, or diverged worktrees intact.\n- **Visual Warnings for Skipped Updates**: Added highlighted console notifications when worktree updates are skipped due to local modifications, unpushed commits, or diverged branches.\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- **tmux Session Server Lookups**: Fixed an issue where new terminal tabs in tmux looked up sessions against the current tmux server socket rather than the default server socket used by the new tab.\n- **Multiplexer Session Termination Safety**: Prevented `on_exists: kill` from terminating unrelated untagged sessions sharing the same name.\n- **Cross-Version tmux Session Names**: Sanitized dots to underscores in tmux session names across all versions to ensure consistent naming and discovery on older tmux releases.\n- **CLI `new_tab` Multiplexer Handling**: Allowed tmux and zellij custom commands configured with `new_tab` to execute in CLI mode by attaching within the active terminal rather than failing.\n- **Herdr Socket and Environment Routing**: Fixed socket routing for ambient Herdr sessions, ensured containerized Herdr tabs fall back to `sh` when `bash` is missing, and preserved existing panes when tabs specify no custom command.\n- **Active Branch Reuse on Worktree Creation**: Handled existing checked-out branches gracefully during pull request worktree creation by returning the active path instead of aborting with an error.\n\n### Maintenance\n\n- Simplified and polished project documentation, CLI references, man pages, and the `README.md` for clarity and consistency (#104).\n- Synchronized the minimum required Go version to Go 1.26 across documentation and project metadata (#104).\n- Addressed linter warnings in the documentation synchronization scripts.\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- Updated `charm.land/bubbletea/v2` to v2.1.0.\n- Updated `github.com/urfave/cli/v3` to v3.14.0.\n- Updated `golang.org/x/sys`, `golang.org/x/term`, `golang.org/x/sync`, and other indirect dependencies to their latest versions.\n"}
